# Token budget rules

## Plan tracking
- Multi-step work follows a plan file under `docs/`. Each finished step is marked `[x]` in the plan file together with its PR link.
- A new agent reads the plan file and only the files that step needs — not earlier chats.
- Files already read in this session and unchanged since are not read again.

## One PR per batch
- Complete the whole requested batch, open a SINGLE PR, report, and stop.
- The report contains: PR link, head SHA, a one-line test summary, and any blocker.
- Do not start extra work just to report CI status or to say "waiting for merge".
- Do not start the next batch on your own.

## Lightweight verification
- While developing, run only the narrow relevant tests.
- Before opening the PR, run: `npm run test:run`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build` (`build` already runs typecheck).
- Read only the summary lines of their output (e.g. `| tail -5`). Open the full log only on failure.

## Screenshots
- Take screenshots only when what the user sees changes: one at 390px, one at desktop width.
- No screenshots for config, SEO, data, or docs-only changes.

## Local Worker runtime
- Use `npx wrangler dev --local` only when routing, headers, or `wrangler.jsonc` change.

## Reporting and context
- Keep reports short. Do not paste full diffs, logs, or file contents into the report.
- Do not dump `node_modules`/`dist` listings or large files into context.

## Session and loop limits
- One session per batch: after opening the PR, end the session. The next batch starts fresh from the plan file and `AGENTS.md`, not from chat history.
- If the same check fails twice after a fix attempt, stop and report the blocker instead of retrying.
- Before starting a batch, post a plan of at most 5 lines (files to touch, checks to run) and wait for approval.

## Quiet output and targeted reads
- Use quiet test output: `npm run test:run -- --reporter=dot`.
- Prefer `grep` and line-range reads over whole-file reads. Do not re-read a file after editing it.
- Do not hand-fix formatting or lint issues that `npx eslint --fix` can fix.

## Scope
- These rules do not relax the quality rules in `AGENTS.md`.
